<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="76967" href="schedule/2022/fall/DANC/116/76967.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2022" href="schedule/2022.xml">2022</calendarYear><term id="120228" href="schedule/2022/fall.xml">Fall 2022</term><subject id="DANC" href="schedule/2022/fall/DANC.xml">Dance</subject><course id="116" href="schedule/2022/fall/DANC/116.xml">Dance I</course></parents><sectionNumber>E  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Dance I: Ballroom</sectionTitle><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course is an introduction to partnering techniques through the lens of popular ballroom and Latin dances (waltz, tango, rumba, cha cha, etc.). This class will also provide cultural contexts of the dances from their European, Latin American, and Afro-Cuban origins to their current, cosmopolitan forms. May be repeated. This section is primarily for non-majors and beginning movers.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2022-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2022-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="B2 ">Laboratory</type><start>05:00 PM</start><end>06:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2500</roomNumber><buildingName>Krannert Center for Perf Arts</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Tecza" firstName="A">Tecza, A</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>